<section class="text-center mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-6">SSI Construction Manager Overview</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-6">For construction and project managers: build budgets, schedules, purchase orders, and invoices, then report to owners and consultants with one click.</p>
  <video class="mx-auto shadow-lg rounded-xl" width="720" height="480" controls preload="metadata" poster="/Screenshot_2.png">
    <source src="/ssi-construction-manager-overview.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    Your browser does not support the video tag.
  </video>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-6 text-left text-gray-600 space-y-3">
    <p>In this walkthrough you'll see how a project comes together end to end. Start by building a divisional cost breakdown using CSI MasterFormat, Uniformat, or your own cost codes, then transfer it straight into a live project budget.</p>
    <p>From there, build a schedule with task dependencies and generate a Gantt chart, issue purchase orders tied to cost codes, and log invoices against those POs so your budget stays current automatically. When it's time to report, generate a PDF for owners or consultants in one click instead of rebuilding it in a spreadsheet.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="text-center mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-6">SSI Trade Manager Overview</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-6">For trades and subcontractors: collaborate directly on projects managed with SSI Construction Manager, at no extra cost when you're already an SSI subscriber.</p>
  <video class="mx-auto shadow-lg rounded-xl" width="480" height="480" controls preload="metadata" poster="/Screenshot_2.png">
    <source src="/ssi-trade-app-overview.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    Your browser does not support the video tag.
  </video>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-6 text-left text-gray-600 space-y-3">
    <p>Trades and subcontractors get their own view into the same project — no separate login for the GC and separate spreadsheet for the trade. From here you can see look-ahead schedules, mark progress against assigned tasks, and comment directly on schedule items instead of chasing updates over email.</p>
    <p>Purchase orders and invoices can be submitted from the same place, and since they're tied to the same cost codes the general contractor is using, nothing gets lost in translation between the trade's paperwork and the project budget. If you're already subscribed to SSI, joining another company's project costs nothing extra.</p>
  </div>
</section>

